card st-model-per-role-role-names  [-]  PROPOSED — not in the map until it is accepted
The held-out step author, the held-out binder and the overseer classifiers have their own role names
why: The model of an agent comes from its role name, so each kind of agent needs a fixed name that the table and the test fake both read. Three kinds had no name yet.

The held-out step author has the role step-author, the held-out binder has the role binder, and the overseer classifiers have the role classifier. Each runs on Sonnet with no advisor.

  -> depends_on      st-build-seam-role-env  Each agent that the pipeline starts carries its role outside the prompt
       why: takes the rule that each kind of agent gets a fixed role name
  -> refines         stages  Three stages: plan, build, validate
